<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Model fidelity to source: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the full 2D off-lattice spatial BARW ductal network simulator with persistent tip migration, Poisson bifurcation (A -> 2A), immutable ductal trail deposition (A -> A + I), and steric/TGF-beta tip-duct annihilation within sensing radius R_a (A + I -> I) (L156-341); solves the 1D mean-field Fisher-KPP travelling-wave BARW PDE system (L348-420); computes exact critical Galton-Watson subtree size distributions P(S = 2n+1) via Catalan numbers (L126-149); and evaluates multi-organ universality across mouse mammary gland, kidney, and pancreas plus TGF-beta / R_a perturbations and R_a = 0 non-annihilating explosion ablation (L427-504). Backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 `sorry`s) in `Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Morphometric validation: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L787-875) reports 8 quantitative morphometrics with reference values, dispersion statistics (RMSE, Pearson r, p-value, SD, CV), and negative-control ablation deltas: 2D BARW topological branching fraction q_branch = 0.480 (3-organ ensemble mean 0.4852 ± 0.0142 vs 0.50 critical point), critical Galton-Watson subtree exponent tau = 1.4418 (log-log r = -0.99990, p = 1.2e-18), generational q_branch(g) relaxation Pearson r = 0.99311 (RMSE = 0.0188, p = 9.76e-9 across mammary/kidney/pancreas), 1D homeostatic wake duct density i_inf = 0.28695 (wake CV = 0.0585 vs 0.28571 reference), attenuated-TGF-beta hyper-branching length ratio = 8.82x (vs 0.19x hypoplasia), R_a = 0 ablation explosion delta (+49 unarrested tips and 556 duct crossovers vs 0 in WT), and exact specimen segmentation (N_term = 34, N_branch = 33, q_branch = 0.4925, peripheral tip r/R_max = 0.7833 ± 0.2582)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-1d-mean-field-barw-homeostatic-wake-duct-density-i-inf>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-2d-barw-self-terminated-topological-branching-fraction-q-branch-wt>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-attenuated-tgf-beta-r-a-1-75-vs-wild-type-r-a-3-5-ductal-hyper-branching-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-critical-galton-watson-subtree-size-power-law-exponent-tau>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-generational-branching-probability-q-branch-g-correlation-across-3-organs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-mouse-branched-ductal-specimen-active-distal-tip-count-n-term>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-mouse-branched-ductal-specimen-peripheral-active-tip-radial-localization-r-r-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-non-annihilating-r-a-0-ablation-unarrested-active-tip-explosion-delta>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — MorphoEval overall 92.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2 remediated) evaluation of `2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py` (92.4/100, up from 51.8/100 in Pass 1; +40.6 overall). The remediated script implements a full 2D off-lattice spatial Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW) ductal tree simulator with persistent tip migration (v_0), Poisson tip bifurcation (A -> 2A at rate k_b), differentiated ductal trail deposition (A -> A + I), and steric/TGF-beta tip-duct annihilation within radius R_a (A + I -> I); verifies exact topological self-termination (N_term = N_branch + 1, q_branch -> 1/2) and universal critical Galton-Watson subtree size scaling P(S) ~ S^(-3/2) across mouse pubertal mammary gland, metanephric kidney, and embryonic pancreas regimes; solves the 1D Fisher-KPP travelling-wave BARW PDE demonstrating active-tip wake extinction (a_wake = 0.00038) and homeostatic duct plateau i_inf = 0.28695 (vs k_b/k_a = 0.28571); evaluates TGF-beta / R_a hyper-branching (R_a = 1.75), hypoplasia (R_a = 7.0), and R_a = 0 non-annihilating explosion ablation (+49 unarrested tips, 556 duct crossovers); segments the SHA-256-verified mouse branched ductal network fluorescence micrograph (`mouse_branched_ductal_network_specimen.jpg`, detecting N_term = 34 active distal buds at peripheral r/R_max = 0.7833 and N_branch = 33 bifurcations, q_branch = 33/67 = 0.4925); and is backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean`. Overall 92.5/100 (faithfulness 92.0, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 95, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/branching_random_walk_annihilation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py at 8871db0, image/png, 1176186 B, 2475×1530 px, artifact_sha256 0c1bc09baee06f93d711f322845926b9e9d8a650e09d2cff65f58c8c8299ced5 (sha256 0c1bc09baee06f93d711f322845926b9e9d8a650e09d2cff65f58c8c8299ced5), spec_fingerprint 8396b081dd41f5428f101435bc6396b6e50c4b756e20f4883dc6ac81bd4c137b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8396b081dd41f5428f101435bc6396b6e50c4b756e20f4883dc6ac81bd4c137b; artifact_sha256: 0c1bc09baee06f93d711f322845926b9e9d8a650e09d2cff65f58c8c8299ced5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/branching_random_walk_annihilation_reference.json=d85ad5c91bd80050..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/mouse_branched_ductal_network_specimen.jpg=d8946f47dcc4d313..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/paper_citations.bib=521cc284892baf9f..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/scout_manifest.json=8b04ea70e9991ba0...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-branching-random-walk-annihilation-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple clonal lineage-tracing neutral drift dynamics within individual terminal end buds (Scheele et al. 2017 Nature) to the macroscopic BARW bifurcating tree.",
        "remediation needed: Extend the 2D off-lattice BARW simulator to 3D cylindrical fat-pad and embryonic mesenchymal geometries with anisotropic extracellular matrix fiber alignment (Bordeu et al. 2023 Nat. Commun.)." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.25e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

